# Grammar
Example Python Grammaer
https://docs.python.org/3/reference/grammar.html

Lexer → tokens
Parser → AST (syntax only)
Resolver/Name analysis (optional) → resolve identifiers, scopes
Type checker / semantic analyzer → verify operand types, return types, immutability rules, etc.
Interpreter or codegen → execute or compile, using the validated AST


Currently, a trivial grammar is implemented:
statement -> expression -> unary -> primary

eventually
statement -> expression -> equality -> comparison -> term -> factor -> unary -> primary

```text
statement  ::= expression ";" | EOF
expression ::= primary
<unary>         ::= ( "!" | "-" ) <unary>
                  | <primary>
primary    ::= NUMBER | STRING | IDENTIFIER
```


Binary operator precedence is encoded by the order: 
logic_or → logic_and → equality → comparison → term → factor → unary → primary (lower to higher precedence).


program node is root of AST, and can only have statements or EOF as child nodes.

statements can only have print, var and expressions as child nodes. Etc.

Terminal nodes cannot have any children.

further, children of a node can be thought of as subclasses of their parent node. In this way, statement is a parent type to all other types.

```text
# Starting Rules
# =================
<program>       ::= <statement>* <EOF>

# General Statements
# ===================
<statement>     ::= "print" <expression> ";" 
                  | "var" <identifier> ( "=" <expression> )? ";" 
                  | <expression> ";"

<expression>    ::= <assignment>

<assignment>    ::= <identifier> "=" <assignment>
                  | <logic_or>

<logic_or>      ::= <logic_and> ( "or" <logic_and> )*

<logic_and>     ::= <equality> ( "and" <equality> )*

<equality>      ::= <comparison> ( ( "!=" | "==" ) <comparison> )*

<comparison>    ::= <term> ( ( ">" | ">=" | "<" | "<=" ) <term> )*

<term>          ::= <factor> ( ( "+" | "-" ) <factor> )*

<factor>        ::= <unary> ( ( "*" | "/" ) <unary> )*

<unary>         ::= ( "!" | "-" ) <unary>
                  | <primary>

<primary>       ::= "true"
                  | "false"
                  | "nil"
                  | <number>
                  | <string>
                  | <identifier>
                  | "(" <expression> ")"

# Terminal Nodes
# ===============
<identifier>    ::= /* lexical token produced by lexer: identifier name */

<number>        ::= /* numeric literal token */

<string>        ::= /* string literal token */

<EOF>           ::= /* end-of-file token */
```


Example Gammar
```text
expression   ::= equality ;
equality     ::= comparison ( ( "==" | "!=" ) comparison )* ;
comparison   ::= term ( ( ">" | ">=" | "<" | "<=" ) term )* ;
term         ::= factor ( ( "+" | "-" ) factor )* ;
factor       ::= unary ( ( "*" | "/" ) unary )* ;
unary        ::= ( "!" | "-" ) unary | primary ;
primary      ::= NUMBER | STRING | "true" | "false" | "nil" | "(" expression ")" ;
```

Generate AST from grammar using lalrpop or pest/peg.


